    "title": "<p class=\"TableTitle\"><strong>Table&nbsp;2.03</strong> Depth of invasion and metastasis in superficial squamous cell carcinoma of the oesophagus</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Marnix Jansen",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; mso-yfti-tbllook: 1184; mso-padding-alt: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 0; mso-yfti-firstrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 135.65pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"181\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Depth</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 314.9pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"420\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210035094;\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Metastasis rate</span></strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 1; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 135.65pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"181\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210035094;\">pTis, pT1a-LPM</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 314.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"420\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210035094;\">0.4% (95%&nbsp;CI: 0&ndash;2.0%) <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{23399555}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 2; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 135.65pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"181\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210035094;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">pT1a-MM</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 314.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"420\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210035094;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">7.5% (95%&nbsp;CI: 4.9&ndash;11.0%) <span class=\"Ref-ID\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">{32072683}</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 3; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 135.65pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"181\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210035094;\">pT1b-SM, &le;&nbsp;200&nbsp;&mu;m</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 314.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"420\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210035094;\">10.4% (95%&nbsp;CI: 5.7&ndash;17.1%)<sup>a</sup> <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{32072683}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 4; mso-yfti-lastrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 135.65pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"181\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210035094;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">pT1b-SM, &gt;&nbsp;200&nbsp;&mu;m</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 314.9pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"420\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210035094;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">15.8% (95%&nbsp;CI: 11.3&ndash;21.3%)<sup>a</sup> <span class=\"Ref-ID\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">{32072683}</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210035094;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">43.8% (95%&nbsp;CI: 31.4&ndash;56.7%)<sup>b</sup> <span class=\"Ref-ID\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">{19903192}</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><sup>a</sup>Data from endoscopically resected cases only. <sup>b</sup>Data from surgically resected cases only.</p>",
    "imageUrl": null,
    "thumbnail": null
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 74747,
    "bookid": 72,
    "chapterId": 13,
    "fileId": 49884,
    "type": "Table",
    "diagnosis": "",
    "title": "<p class=\"TableTitle\"><strong>Box&nbsp;2.02</strong> Risk factors for oesophageal squamous cell carcinoma</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Marnix Jansen",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 446.55pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; border-collapse: collapse; mso-yfti-tbllook: 1184; mso-padding-alt: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" border=\"0\" width=\"595\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 0; mso-yfti-firstrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid; height: 10.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 446.55pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 10.2pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"595\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Tobacco use<sup>a</sup></span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 1; page-break-inside: avoid; height: 98.45pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 446.55pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 98.45pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"595\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Smoking or chewing is the most important risk factor in high-income countries <span class=\"Ref-ID\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">{39550174;18679388;28823862}</span></span>; much weaker factor in low-incidence areas</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Risk is dependent on both intensity and duration of use, with cessation being associated with decreasing risk after 5&nbsp;years and a return to the baseline risk level of a lifelong non-smoker after 10&ndash;20&nbsp;years</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Tobacco-specific nitrosamines and polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbons are believed to be the main carcinogenic substances <span class=\"Ref-ID\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">{28823862}</span></span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 2; page-break-inside: avoid; height: 17.15pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 446.55pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.15pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"595\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Alcohol consumption<sup>a</sup></span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 3; page-break-inside: avoid; height: 152.45pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 446.55pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 152.45pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"595\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Consumption of &gt;&nbsp;3 drinks per day is associated with a risk almost 5&nbsp;times that in individuals who consume &le;&nbsp;1 drink per day <span class=\"Ref-ID\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">{18679388;28823862}</span></span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">The mechanism of carcinogenesis remains uncertain, but acetaldehyde, a metabolite of ethanol, is a known carcinogen capable of causing DNA abnormalities and structural and functional alterations to protein <span class=\"Ref-ID\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">{28823862}</span></span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><em><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">ALDH2</span></em><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\"> and <em>ALDH1A1</em> mutations, which are found almost exclusively in eastern Asian populations, lead to the accumulation of acetaldehyde following the consumption of alcohol. These mutations are associated with a dose-dependent increase in the risk of oesophageal squamous cell carcinoma. For example, heterozygous and homozygous <em>ALDH2</em> mutations, respectively, are associated with risks 4&nbsp;times and 13&nbsp;times that in individuals without <em>ALDH2</em> mutation <span class=\"Ref-ID\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">{17674367}</span></span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 4; page-break-inside: avoid; height: 17.15pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 446.55pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.15pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"595\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Drinking very hot beverages<sup>b</sup></span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 5; page-break-inside: avoid; height: 17.15pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 446.55pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.15pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"595\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Drinking hot beverages such as tea or mat&eacute; appears to be an important risk factor in Uruguay, southern Brazil, northern Argentina, the United Republic of Tanzania, and the Islamic Republic of Iran <span class=\"Ref-ID\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">{18679388;28823862}</span></span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 6; page-break-inside: avoid; height: 17.15pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 446.55pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.15pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"595\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Genetic factors</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 7; page-break-inside: avoid; height: 17.15pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 446.55pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.15pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"595\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Several genetic diseases (e.g. tylosis, a keratosis disorder caused by an autosomal dominant mutation in <em>RHBDF2</em> at 17q25.3 <span class=\"Ref-ID\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">{18679388;22265016}</span></span>, and Fanconi anaemia <span class=\"Ref-ID\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">{28823862}</span></span>)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 8; page-break-inside: avoid; height: 17.15pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 446.55pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.15pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"595\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Associated medical conditions</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 9; page-break-inside: avoid; height: 64.8pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 446.55pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 64.8pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"595\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Plummer&ndash;Vinson syndrome</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Achalasia</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Radiotherapy to the chest area</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Caustic ingestion injury <span class=\"Ref-ID\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">{18679388;28823862}</span></span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 10; page-break-inside: avoid; height: 17.15pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 446.55pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.15pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"595\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Other</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 11; page-break-inside: avoid; height: 81.55pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 446.55pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 81.55pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"595\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Advancing age</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Male sex (the association is potentially weaker than squamous cell carcinoma)</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">X-ray and gamma radiation</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Opium consumption<sup>b</sup></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Consumption of pickled vegetables<sup>b</sup></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 12; page-break-inside: avoid; height: 17.15pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 446.55pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.15pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"595\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Unlikely to be a risk factor: HPV infection</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 13; mso-yfti-lastrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid; height: 17.15pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 446.55pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.15pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"595\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">The current consensus is that there is no evidence for HPV infection as a risk factor for the development of oesophageal squamous cell carcinoma <span class=\"Ref-ID\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">{28052061}</span></span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><sup>a</sup>These risk factors have sufficient evidence of oesophageal carcinogenicity. <sup>b</sup>These risk factors have emerging evidence for oesophageal carcinogenicity.</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">References: <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{23189752;23193840;31310458;36395294;8411630}</span>.</p>",
    "imageUrl": null,
    "thumbnail": null
  },
